# Ralph progress: stamps-monetization

## Codebase Patterns

- Netlify Database migrations live in
  `netlify/database/migrations/<number>_<name>/migration.sql`.
- Reversible migrations can include a sibling `down.sql` rollback file.
- Schema tests use Vitest and read migration SQL as text from
  `netlify/database/migrations`.
- `tsconfig.json` includes `vitest/globals` because many existing tests use
  global Vitest APIs such as `expect`.
- Stamp accounting services use `getDatabase().pool.connect()` and explicit
  `BEGIN`/`COMMIT` transactions when multiple writes must stay consistent.
- Stamp debit should atomically update `stamp_lots` using a nested
  `SELECT ... FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED`, then update `users.stamps_balance`
  with a `stamps_balance > 0` guard in the same transaction.
- Failed-send refunds re-credit the original `stamp_lots` row and cached
  `users.stamps_balance`, then record a `failed_send_refund` transaction.
- Autumn stamp pack product ids, counts, prices, and product metadata live in
  shared `PACK_DEFINITIONS` in `src/stamp-packs.ts`; `netlify/lib/billing.ts`
  re-exports it for backend callers.
- Autumn webhook processing lives in `applyAutumnWebhookEvent`; stamp pack
  `checkout.completed` events are handled before subscription status events,
  and purchase idempotency checks `stamp_transactions.reference_id`.
- Stamp pack purchase UI lives in shared `BuyPackModal` under
  `src/components`; routes should open it via `State.OpenBuyPackModal`.
- Current user data from `/api/whoami` includes optional `stamps_balance`;
  send gating should check an explicit zero balance and allow unknown balances.
- Checkout account creation is centralized in
  `upsertCheckoutUser`; signup-only side effects should use its
  insert-or-select result so existing checkout users are not reprocessed.
- One-time stamp backfills live in `netlify/lib/stamp-backfill.ts`, check
  `stamp_transactions.reason = 'migration_grant'` per user for idempotency,
  and call `creditStampLot` with `transactionReason: 'migration_grant'`.
- The postcard send route uses `POST /api/posts`: validate drawing
  ownership with `userOwnsDrawing`, then call `debitStamp` before
  `publishDrawing`; the stamp transaction reference currently uses the
  drawing id as the send reference.
- Post-debit failures in `POST /api/posts` should call `refundFailedSend`
  with the debited lot id and return the delivery refund message from the
  API response so the send route can show it as an alert.
- Stamp UI should use the shared `IconStamp` component from
  `src/components/icon-stamp.ts` so later balance, send-cost, and stamp page
  treatments share the same icon language.
- Stamp refund previews should use `calculateStampLotRefundCents`; it floors
  the multiply-first prorated purchase refund and returns zero for grants,
  gifts, missing prices, and fully used lots.
- User-initiated stamp refunds run through `refundPurchasedStampLot`, which
  locks the caller-owned lot, writes local refund state in one transaction,
  and receives an injected Autumn refund function so API tests can verify
  rollback behavior without calling Autumn.
- Stamp lot refund UI should load lots through `State.FetchStampLots`, submit
  refunds through `State.RefundStampLot`, and use `/api/stamps/lots` for
  refund preview rows calculated server-side.
- Existing-recipient stamp gifts start through
  `/api/stamps/gifts/checkout`, attach gift sender and recipient metadata to
  the Autumn checkout, and are credited from the checkout webhook.
- Gift webhook handling uses `creditGiftStampLot` so recipient
  `gift_received` credit and sender `gift_sent` history rows are written in
  one stamp transaction while leaving the sender balance unchanged.
- Gift purchase UI lives in `GiftStampsPanel` and starts checkout through
  `State.StartGiftStampCheckout`, keeping stamp checkout state methods on the
  central State object.
- Pending non-user gifts are stored in `pending_gifts`, created from the
  Autumn checkout webhook, and loaded with stamp lots through
  `/api/stamps/lots` so the sender stamps panel can show them.
- Non-user gift checkout uses `gift_pending_recipient_email` metadata while
  existing-user gifts continue to use `gift_recipient_user_id` metadata.
- Pending gifts are claimed in the checkout signup path for newly inserted
  users; the normal signup grant is applied first, then matching
  `pending_gifts` rows are credited as `gift_received` and marked claimed.
- Scheduled stamp maintenance jobs can use Netlify's `schedule()` wrapper in
  `netlify/functions`, while keeping the DB workflow in `netlify/lib/stamps.ts`
  with injected Autumn and Resend functions to avoid billing/stamp import
  cycles.
- Sender gift management uses recipient `stamp_lots` rows with
  `source = 'gift_received'` and `gifted_by_user_id` set to the sender; the
  sender stamps panel loads those rows through `/api/stamps/lots` as
  `sent_gifts`.
- Gift reclaim refunds write `stamp_transactions.reason = 'gift_reclaimed'`
  against the recipient's lot and balance, while Autumn refunds the original
  gift checkout to the sender's payment method.

